  draft §2.7/§3.3.3 preconditions actually fire: the IDENTITY public
  key is rejected by `verify`/`popVerify`/`aggregateVerify`
  (KeyValidate), and an on-curve NON-SUBGROUP `G2` point (crafted via
  `mapToCurveG2` WITHOUT cofactor clearing; its non-membership asserted
  in the test) is rejected as a signature by `verify`/`popVerify`/
  `aggregateVerify`/`fastAggregateVerify` (signature_subgroup_check) —
  all returning `false`, never panicking.
- An 8-signer aggregate (9 pairing terms) crossing
  `coreAggregateVerify`'s stack-chunked Miller-accumulator boundary,
  accept + cross-boundary tamper reject.

